# Rasa Skills / Maestro (Telano)

This repo is a **calm_v2 / Maestro Skills** project. Do not introduce CALM v1
artifacts (`config.yml`, `domain.yml`, flow YAMLs under `data/`, classic
`credentials.yml` / `endpoints.yml`).

## First commands

```bash
make verify
make train
make inspect
```

Prefer `make` targets over raw `uv run rasa …`.

## Layout

- Root: `agent.yml`, `integrations.yml`, `memory.yml`, `responses.yml`
- One skill per folder under `skills/<id>/`
- Shared tools in `tools/telco.py` via `import_tools`
- Demo backend in `lib/database.py` + `data/source/*.json`

## Progressive control order

prose → `tool_constraints` → scoped `if:` → verbatim `utter:` → `ordered_block`

Showcase skill: `reset_router` (remote factory reset).

## Skill authoring rules

- Boolean `if:` expressions use Python `True`/`False`, not YAML booleans
- `description:` only on llm_settable / collect-owned memory fields
- Side effects need confirmation (`requires_confirmation`) when irreversible
- Keep voice copy short
- Compose with `@skill.<name>` instead of growing monolithic skills

## Secrets

Never commit `.env`. Document vars only in `.env.example`.
Makefile may `-include .env` for presence checks but must **not** `export` it.
